      "message": "Fun thing here is that `strncmp(argv[1], \"debugger\", sizeof(\"debugger\"))` is not more secure than `strcmp()` version. \n\nThe problem will appear when `argv[1]` is not null terminated string, shorter than `\"debugger\"` string. To avoid reading after the end of the `argv[1]` string we should pass size of `argv[1]` to `strncmp()` (it will work because we are guaranteed that \"debugger\" ends with null character).\n\nNIT: You can extend commit message with information, why `strncmp()` is not better than `strcmp()` in this case.",
